    (1557,1529,'Category IV patient who has been transferred from another register for treatment of drug-resistant TB to continue Category IV treatment. His/her outcome should be reported to the transferring unit so that it can report his/her outcome in the cohort in which s/he originally started Category IV treatment. This group is excluded from the quarterly reports of the receiving unti on registration and treatment result. (Definition from World Health Organization Guidelines for the programmatic management of drug-resistant TB)','en',6,'2006-08-23 16:12:20.0',12,null,'ed283dde-07fe-102c-b5fa-0017a47871b2'),
    (1558,1530,'Patient that does not fit into any of the following categories - new, relapse, treatment after default, treatment after failure of first treatment, treatment after failure of re-treatment, or transfer in. This group includes Category IV patients who were treated outside DOTS programs and for whom the outcome of the latest treatment is unknown. (Definition from World Health Organization Guidelines for the programmatic management of drug-resistant TB)','en',1,'2006-08-23 16:15:16.0',24839,null,'ed28405e-07fe-102c-b5fa-0017a47871b2'),
