    (1646,1624,'A test of thyroid stimulating hormone levels that is often the test of choice for evaluating thyroid function and/or symptoms of hyper- or hypothyroidism.','en',6,'2006-09-11 20:17:57.0',24839,'2012-09-26 20:32:50.0','eceb3858-07fe-102c-b5fa-0017a47871b2'),
    (1647,1625,'A creatinine clearance test measures how well creatinine is removed from blood by the kidneys. A creatinine clearance test is performed both on a blood sample taken from a vein and on a sample of urine collected over 24 hours (24-hour urine sample). (Definition from health.yahoo.com)','en',24839,'2006-09-11 14:21:14.0',7,null,'eceb39b6-07fe-102c-b5fa-0017a47871b2'),
    (1648,1626,'A bicarbonate (HCO3) test measures the level of bicarbonate in the blood','en',12,'2006-09-11 14:24:57.0',7,null,'eceb3b28-07fe-102c-b5fa-0017a47871b2'),
    (1649,1627,'Test in which a sample of urine is prepared in the laboratory and a drop of the urine sediment is put onto a glass slide. The sediment is then examined under a microscope to identify casts, crystals, squamous (flat) cells, and other large objects.','en',1,'2006-09-11 14:57:47.0',7,null,'eceb3c86-07fe-102c-b5fa-0017a47871b2'),
    (1650,1628,'Constipation usually is defined as fewer than three bowel movements per week. Severe constipation is defined as less than one bowel movement per week.  (Definition from www.medinenet.com)','en',12,'2006-09-11 21:22:58.0',24839,'2011-08-08 19:55:42.0','eceb3dee-07fe-102c-b5fa-0017a47871b2'),
    (1651,1629,'Change in skin color on the spectrum from pink to brownish-black. Usually an unwanted side effect of medication.','en',6,'2006-09-11 15:30:12.0',6,null,'eceb3f56-07fe-102c-b5fa-0017a47871b2'),
    (1652,1630,'A ringing, swishing, or other type of noise that seems to originate in the ear or head. (Definition from www.medicinenet.com)','en',6,'2006-09-11 21:31:15.0',1,'2011-11-17 15:52:08.0','eceb40b4-07fe-102c-b5fa-0017a47871b2'),
    (1653,1631,'Tremor is a rhythmic, involuntary muscular contraction characterized by oscillations of a part of the body. (Definition from www.medicinenet.com)','en',6,'2006-09-11 15:32:44.0',1,null,'eceb4212-07fe-102c-b5fa-0017a47871b2'),
    (1654,1632,'A harmful or abnormal result to an anti-tuberculous medication. An adverse effect may be caused by administration of a medication or by exposure to a chemical and be indicated by an untoward result such as by illness or death.','en',12,'2006-09-11 15:34:31.0',7,null,'eceb437a-07fe-102c-b5fa-0017a47871b2'),
    (1655,1633,'A thiosaemicarbazone that is used in association with other antimycobacterial agents in the initial and continuation phases of antituberculosis regimens','en',12,'2006-09-11 15:42:29.0',12,null,'ed1fdb30-07fe-102c-b5fa-0017a47871b2'),
    (1656,1634,'Terizidone is a combination of two cycloserine molecules. It is an anti-tuberculous drug used in treating multidrug-resistant TB.  TERIZIDONE is considered effective in the treatment of TB and may also be useful for the treatment of urinary tract infections including those due to TB. It is recommended for the treatment of MDR-TB patients in both the intensive and continuation phases. Oral bacteriostatic second-line TB med.','en',12,'2006-09-11 15:46:45.0',1,'2011-11-09 11:35:54.0','ed210af0-07fe-102c-b5fa-0017a47871b2'),
