    (2409,2617,'A low level of potassium in the blood. Potassium is an electrolyte that is important to the function of the nerve and muscle cells, including the heart. Hypokalemia is most common in people with diseases that affect kidney function, people who take diuretics, people with eating disorders, or a reaction to TB medicine.','en',7,'2007-08-17 10:41:32.0',6,null,'ecf3af2e-07fe-102c-b5fa-0017a47871b2'),
