    (5166,6691,'Type 1 diabetes is usually diagnosed in children and young adults, and was previously known as juvenile diabetes. In type 1 diabetes, the body does not produce insulin.','en',7,'2010-03-02 17:28:49.0',6,null,'a50124c9-c84b-425b-a4c6-22f0207ec3b1'),
    (5167,6692,'Type 2 diabetes is the most common form of diabetes.  In type 2 diabetes, either the body does not produce enough insulin or the cells ignore the insulin. ','en',7,'2010-03-02 17:30:20.0',24839,null,'372feefc-2433-4cc3-9231-74defff95bd3'),
