    (5308,6848,'Secondary hypertension (or, less commonly, inessential hypertension) is a type of hypertension  which by definition is caused by an identifiable underlying secondary cause. It is much less common than the other type, called essential hypertension, affecting only 5% of hypertensive patients. It has many different causes including endocrine diseases, kidney diseases, and tumors. It also can be a side effect of many medications.','en',7,'2010-07-30 16:44:31.0',24839,null,'bc28e726-6ba3-4196-a4f0-6939bf3c76d0'),
